; `restrict(no-escape)` (docs/memory-model-v2-design.md §2.7): the
; declaration stores nothing it allocates into any of its parameters.
; It rides the restriction rail every other claim rides, and reads the
; region facts (typecheck.ax, `restrictNoEscape`) rather than the
; effect row.
;
;   1  `stores` pushes a string it allocated onto its parameter, and
;      the store is made by `vecPush`: AX3049, naming the parameter
;      and the callee the value went in through.
;   2  `reads` answers a length: SILENT, proven.
;   3  `dispatch` calls its own parameter, so where its allocations
;      flow is decided by the caller: AX3051, a warning.
;   4  `dispatchStrict` is the same body under `strict`: AX3057.
;
; The facts are the same ones the escape rule consults, so a claim
; here is checked by the analysis that also refuses AX3060 - one
; computation, two readers.
(import Vec)

(import Str)

;@axiom:restrict(no-escape)
(:: stores (-> (Vec String) String Int))

(fn (stores v x)
  {
    (vecPush v (strConcat x "!"))
    0
  }
)

;@axiom:restrict(no-escape)
(:: reads (-> (Vec String) Int))

(fn (reads v) (vecLen v))

;@axiom:restrict(no-escape)
(:: dispatch (-> (-> String Int) String Int))

(fn (dispatch f s) (f s))

;@axiom:restrict(no-escape, strict)
(:: dispatchStrict (-> (-> String Int) String Int))

(fn (dispatchStrict f s) (f s))

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) 0)
